cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "orca-engine: a streaming parser and thermochemistry engine for ORCA output files"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hasan
    given-names: Salam
    email: salamhasan199904@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/salamhasan/orca-engine"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
keywords:
  - computational chemistry
  - quantum chemistry
  - ORCA
  - density functional theory
  - thermochemistry
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  orca-engine is a dependency-free Python library that parses ORCA 5 and ORCA 6
  quantum chemistry output files in a single streaming pass and computes
  reaction energies and bond dissociation energies. It records the level of
  theory, charge, multiplicity, temperature and pressure of every calculation
  and uses them to check that a requested reaction is atom balanced, charge
  balanced, and computed at a single consistent level of theory before
  reporting an energy. The parser is designed around failure modes that produce
  plausible but incorrect numbers rather than errors, including frontier
  orbitals drawn from different geometry optimization steps, atomic-unit
  coordinates reported as Angstrom, and error terminations masked by a
  subsequent rerun.
